<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Planting keep sales slow.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Planting keep sales slow.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Active spring wheat and barley planting, rather than sharply lower cash wheat bids, kept cash wheat sales light in the northern Plains and Pacific Northwest wheat markets Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Minneapolis dealers said wheat sales had been slow prior to Monday's drop in the markets. &quot;It worse now with the board down,&quot; a Minneapolis dealer said.</p>
<p>Planting was under way in nearly all areas except the Red River Valley, where wet fields delayed sowing.</p>
<p>&quot;Out here they are busy putting in spring wheat and barley,&quot; a Montana dealer said.  </p>
